    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly are delighted to present No. 31 Reginald Street, a charming two-bedroom, one-bathroom mid-terraced late Victorian residence, ideally positioned within a quiet residential enclave in the heart of Dublin 8.\r\n\r\nThis beautifully presented red-brick period home offers bright and spacious accommodation arranged over two floors. The ground floor comprises an entrance porch, stylish living room with feature fireplace, inner lobby, fully fitted kitchen and bathroom. Upstairs, there are two bedrooms, comprising one double and one single.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the property benefits from a private walled patio, while residents also enjoy ample on-street permit parking to the front.\r\n\r\nMore about the location...\r\n\r\nReginald Street forms part of a historic neighbourhood dating from the early 1880s, developed by the Dublin Artisan's Dwelling Company under the chairmanship of philanthropist and brewer Edward Cecil Guinness. Today, the area combines its rich architectural heritage with an exciting and evolving urban environment.\r\n\r\nThe property is perfectly positioned close to Francis Street, Meath Street, Thomas Street and the Coombe, with an excellent selection of independent shops, artisan cafés, restaurants and bars nearby. The locality has benefited from significant regeneration, with further exciting developments planned, including the regeneration of the Guinness Brewery and the Iveagh Market.\r\n\r\nExcellent transport links are close at hand, including the LUAS, Dublin Bikes, Heuston and Connolly Stations, together with numerous bus routes providing easy access throughout the city and to Dublin Airport.\r\n\r\nWithin comfortable walking distance of St Stephen’s Green, Christchurch, St Patrick’s Park, Grafton Street and St James’s Hospital, No. 31 Reginald Street presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a characterful period home in one of Dublin 8’s most established and vibrant neighbourhoods."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch (1.45m x 1.1m)\r\nWith tiled flooring. Inner door to the living room\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nElegantly proportioned living room with a feature cast iron fireplace and solid wood flooring.\r\n\r\nInner Hall (1.72m x 1.6m)\r\nFeaturing under-stair storage.\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen (3.2m x 1.78m)\r\nExcellent range of built in wall and floor units complemented by a tiled splash back and tiled floor. Integrated appliance to include a gas hob, electric oven and extractor fan. Door to the rear patio.\r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom (1.63m x 1.57m)\r\nExtensively tiled with a wc, whb and original cast iron bath with overhead electric shower.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (3.94m x 3.09m)\r\nDouble bedroom overlooking the front of the property with an excellent range of built in wardrobes. Laminate flooring. Attic access with pull down step ladder.\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (3m x 2.1m)\r\nSingle bedroom with built in wardrobes and study desk.. Laminate flooring.\r\n\r\n* ALL MEASUREMENTS ARE APPROXIMATE AND FOR GUIDANCE PURPOSES ONLY *"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming late Victorian red-brick period residence.\r\nTwo-bedroom, one-bathroom mid-terraced home.\r\nBright and spacious accommodation over two floors.\r\nStylish living room with feature fireplace.\r\nFully fitted kitchen and well-appointed bathroom.\r\nPrivate walled terraced patio to the rear.\r\nGas Fired Central Heating.\r\nDouble glazed windows.\r\nAmple on-street resident permit parking.\r\nPrime Dublin 8 location close to LUAS, Heuston Station, Grafton Street and an excellent range of local amenities"
      },
      {
